{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/sec-witt-vector-lifting","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Prose","doco:Section"],"label":"sec:witt-vector-lifting","kind":"prose","text":"witt-vector-lifting-intro.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"sec:witt-vector-lifting\"></a><p>The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}_p</code> realisation provides a QOU over characteristic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0</code>. The <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{F}_p</code> realisation provides one over characteristic <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>. The <em>Witt vector functor</em> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">W</code> and the theory of formal groups over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code>-adic rings mediate the passage between them.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/models-of-qous/witt-vector-lifting-intro.md","heading":""}
